WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.375 --> 00:00:03.198
(electronic whoosh)

00:00:03.198 --> 00:00:05.162
- Nothing is impossible.

00:00:05.162 --> 00:00:07.147
- Impossible is just a word.

00:00:07.147 --> 00:00:08.854
- None of this was possible.

00:00:08.854 --> 00:00:09.973
- Ask the impossible.

00:00:09.973 --> 00:00:11.315
- The impossible can happen.

00:00:11.315 --> 00:00:13.388
(bright acoustic guitar)

00:00:13.388 --> 00:00:14.858
Hello Believe Nation, it's Evan,

00:00:14.858 --> 00:00:17.726
my one word is believe,
and I believe in people

00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:19.803
more than they believe in themselves

00:00:19.803 --> 00:00:23.460
and my sincere hope is
that if you see in yourself

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.145
what I see in you, you'll be
able to change the planet.

00:00:27.145 --> 00:00:28.507
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:28.507 --> 00:00:32.048
today we're going to learn
how to do the impossible.

00:00:32.048 --> 00:00:33.143
And as always, if you hear something that

00:00:33.143 --> 00:00:35.112
really resonates with you, please leave it

00:00:35.112 --> 00:00:37.084
down in the comments below
and put quotes around it

00:00:37.084 --> 00:00:38.941
so other people can be inspired,

00:00:38.941 --> 00:00:40.663
and if you're leaving a comment within the

00:00:40.663 --> 00:00:42.257
first few hours of this video going live,

00:00:42.257 --> 00:00:43.786
you have a chance to win one of

00:00:43.786 --> 00:00:45.937
two daily prizes that we have.

00:00:45.937 --> 00:00:47.529
Good luck.

00:00:47.529 --> 00:00:51.112
(soaring orchestral music)

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.205
- As a child, my parents always told me

00:01:00.205 --> 00:01:01.521
you can be whatever you want to be,

00:01:01.521 --> 00:01:03.556
you can do whatever you want to do,

00:01:03.556 --> 00:01:07.349
and you know that office, that position,

00:01:07.349 --> 00:01:10.694
at the highest office on
the face of the Earth,

00:01:10.694 --> 00:01:13.166
it was something, I heard
my parents sayin' it,

00:01:13.166 --> 00:01:14.712
but I didn't totally believe it.

00:01:14.712 --> 00:01:16.859
Yet I went out in the
world and I carried myself

00:01:16.859 --> 00:01:18.623
and I held my head high, and I stood there

00:01:18.623 --> 00:01:20.416
and I looked people in their eyes,

00:01:20.416 --> 00:01:22.676
and I talked to people
as if I was deserving

00:01:22.676 --> 00:01:25.471
of everything that this
planet has to offer.

00:01:25.471 --> 00:01:28.471
(audience applause)

00:01:31.189 --> 00:01:32.022
Thank you.

00:01:32.022 --> 00:01:34.639
I really want to say to children out there

00:01:34.639 --> 00:01:37.471
and to people who are watching,

00:01:37.471 --> 00:01:41.295
Confucius said one time,
"he who says he can,

00:01:41.295 --> 00:01:46.067
"and he who says he can't,
are both usually right."

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:50.507
So I want to stand here before
you and as I hold this award,

00:01:50.507 --> 00:01:52.960
I want to give love to
my wife, and I want you

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.658
to keep in your hearts,
just know that you can.

00:01:55.658 --> 00:01:56.878
Know that you can.

00:01:56.878 --> 00:02:01.336
- Nothing, absolutely
nothing, is impossible.

00:02:01.336 --> 00:02:03.588
You can begin again.

00:02:03.588 --> 00:02:05.838
You can believe God again.

00:02:05.838 --> 00:02:07.766
You can trust again.

00:02:07.766 --> 00:02:09.663
You can be successful.

00:02:09.663 --> 00:02:12.791
You can overcome your addictions.

00:02:12.791 --> 00:02:13.874
You can heal.

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:17.217
You can feel alive again.

00:02:18.791 --> 00:02:22.958
This is when you realize that
those things are possible,

00:02:23.822 --> 00:02:26.330
you are getting a breakthrough.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:30.228
So, I want to encourage you right now,

00:02:30.228 --> 00:02:31.615
don't give in.

00:02:31.615 --> 00:02:33.702
Go for it, don't give up.

00:02:33.702 --> 00:02:36.652
Don't throw in the towel, and even if

00:02:36.652 --> 00:02:39.411
your back is up against the wall,

00:02:39.411 --> 00:02:42.395
even if you are on the ropes, and you

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:47.227
are receiving a rope-a-dope
financially, listen!

00:02:47.227 --> 00:02:49.060
You got to fight back.

00:02:50.192 --> 00:02:52.683
You don't get in life what you want,

00:02:52.683 --> 00:02:55.077
you get what you fight for.

00:02:55.077 --> 00:02:57.860
And when you decide that my future,

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:02.375
my health, my marriage,
my freedom, my happiness,

00:03:02.375 --> 00:03:06.542
my joy, my peace, my children
is worth fighting for,

00:03:07.445 --> 00:03:10.679
you are securing your breakthrough.

00:03:10.679 --> 00:03:12.910
- Just to go after it, I mean, the thing

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:16.377
about being an entrepreneur
is, it's just all to you.

00:03:16.377 --> 00:03:18.360
You know, a lot of people
like to make excuses,

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:19.689
"I don't have connections,
I don't have money,

00:03:19.689 --> 00:03:22.418
"I don't have this," but
you know, if you find

00:03:22.418 --> 00:03:25.339
something that you like
to do or love to do,

00:03:25.339 --> 00:03:28.042
be great at it, and see if you
can turn it into a business,

00:03:28.042 --> 00:03:30.103
and worst case, you're
going to have fun doing

00:03:30.103 --> 00:03:31.591
what it is you love to
do, and best case you can

00:03:31.591 --> 00:03:32.642
turn it into a business.

00:03:32.642 --> 00:03:35.869
I'm just not big on excuses,
I just think if you're really,

00:03:35.869 --> 00:03:37.827
everybody has an opportunity to go for it,

00:03:37.827 --> 00:03:38.660
they just got to do it.

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:40.038
- Here's maybe the greatest thing a teen,

00:03:40.038 --> 00:03:44.404
or anyone in this room and
who's watching on the television

00:03:44.404 --> 00:03:47.759
at home can learn from the champ.

00:03:47.759 --> 00:03:50.069
These are words to remember when anyone

00:03:50.069 --> 00:03:52.363
tries to tell you to give
up, tell you to give in,

00:03:52.363 --> 00:03:55.348
because whatever you're
trying to do is impossible.

00:03:55.348 --> 00:03:59.859
The champ said this:
"Impossible is just a word

00:03:59.859 --> 00:04:03.382
"thrown around by small
men who find it easier

00:04:03.382 --> 00:04:05.358
"to live in the world they've been given

00:04:05.358 --> 00:04:08.360
"than to explore the power
they have to change it.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:10.238
"Impossible is not a fact.

00:04:10.238 --> 00:04:11.666
"It's an opinion.

00:04:11.666 --> 00:04:13.845
"Impossible is potential.

00:04:13.845 --> 00:04:15.530
"Impossible is temporary.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:16.505
(audience applause)

00:04:16.505 --> 00:04:18.646
"Impossible is nothing."

00:04:18.646 --> 00:04:21.818
(audience applause)

00:04:21.818 --> 00:04:23.328
Greatest quote ever.

00:04:23.328 --> 00:04:26.253
(audience applause)

00:04:26.253 --> 00:04:29.753
As a relatively new dad and a former teen,

00:04:31.236 --> 00:04:34.352
I'm here to say you will
make mistakes along the way.

00:04:34.352 --> 00:04:36.079
You will fall down.

00:04:36.079 --> 00:04:37.734
I have many times.

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:39.248
Even Ali did.

00:04:39.248 --> 00:04:43.060
But what we do after that
fall is how we make history

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:45.445
because impossible is nothing.

00:04:45.445 --> 00:04:46.881
- I don't really need the money,

00:04:46.881 --> 00:04:48.750
like I don't need the money anymore.

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:52.000
I've made dream money from video games.

00:04:53.079 --> 00:04:56.053
Like stuff that I, things I
would have never imagined.

00:04:56.053 --> 00:04:59.834
You know, when people say like,
"Is this what you dreamt?"

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:00.944
I didn't dream any of this!

00:05:00.944 --> 00:05:02.686
None of this was possible,

00:05:02.686 --> 00:05:05.948
or even considered
reality when I was a kid.

00:05:05.948 --> 00:05:07.576
You know, when I started skating,

00:05:07.576 --> 00:05:11.557
the best you could hope for
was your picture in a magazine,

00:05:11.557 --> 00:05:13.162
maybe a pro board.

00:05:13.162 --> 00:05:14.097
Maybe.

00:05:14.097 --> 00:05:16.168
And, free gear, that's it.

00:05:16.168 --> 00:05:17.902
And then once you reach
an age of responsibility,

00:05:17.902 --> 00:05:19.959
and this is, I'm talking
about when I was like 12.

00:05:19.959 --> 00:05:22.916
Once you reach an age of
responsibility, say 18,

00:05:22.916 --> 00:05:25.779
your career's over, 'cause
you can't make money doing it,

00:05:25.779 --> 00:05:27.903
you can't enter adult life.

00:05:27.903 --> 00:05:29.408
- I'm a believer, bro.

00:05:29.408 --> 00:05:33.553
Like, I see things, and
I want to make them real.

00:05:33.553 --> 00:05:36.746
No matter how hard it takes,
no matter what obstacles,

00:05:36.746 --> 00:05:41.202
no matter how many embarrassing
meetings I have to imagine,

00:05:41.202 --> 00:05:42.618
it's happening when I leave.

00:05:42.618 --> 00:05:44.182
(interviewer laughs)

00:05:44.182 --> 00:05:46.410
Doesn't matter, I'm a doer,

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:48.625
and a freakin' make-it-happener.

00:05:48.625 --> 00:05:50.115
- I learned a lot from our founders,

00:05:50.115 --> 00:05:51.912
and one of the things I learned was,

00:05:51.912 --> 00:05:54.719
ask the impossible and really dream big.

00:05:54.719 --> 00:05:57.369
What you learn about
people, is if you paint

00:05:57.369 --> 00:06:00.043
a very broad vision, you attract people

00:06:00.043 --> 00:06:01.627
who really want to make it happen.

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:03.216
'Cause they're dreamers too.

00:06:03.216 --> 00:06:05.579
So you can inspire people,
and with that inspiration,

00:06:05.579 --> 00:06:07.182
you're going to get to
the smartest people,

00:06:07.182 --> 00:06:08.959
then they deal with a lot of stuff.

00:06:08.959 --> 00:06:10.977
- But can an organization like Google,

00:06:10.977 --> 00:06:14.263
which espouses the idea that
you're going to give people

00:06:14.263 --> 00:06:17.411
in the organization 15 or
20% of their time to do

00:06:17.411 --> 00:06:20.134
almost anything they want
in terms of innovation,

00:06:20.134 --> 00:06:22.469
can that system work in smaller companies,

00:06:22.469 --> 00:06:24.295
can that system work in any company,

00:06:24.295 --> 00:06:26.010
is that a leadership
canon that can work across

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:27.729
a broad range of companies?

00:06:27.729 --> 00:06:29.784
- Well, in fact, it worked at
Google when Google was tiny.

00:06:29.784 --> 00:06:32.360
So the answer is yes, it
does work in small companies.

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:33.620
Remember, we give this to engineers,

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:36.043
and engineers are not that clever, right?

00:06:36.043 --> 00:06:38.642
If they're going to work on
something in their 20% time,

00:06:38.642 --> 00:06:41.969
it's going to be something
that's pretty related

00:06:41.969 --> 00:06:43.958
to their training and their knowledge.

00:06:43.958 --> 00:06:46.129
And that's why it's so powerful.

00:06:46.129 --> 00:06:48.733
Very very few people
get off the reservation

00:06:48.733 --> 00:06:49.992
and do something completely different

00:06:49.992 --> 00:06:51.956
from technology and so forth.

00:06:51.956 --> 00:06:53.639
And if they did, we would encourage it.

00:06:53.639 --> 00:06:56.074
- Has something manifested,
that you can recall,

00:06:56.074 --> 00:06:59.094
come from just that kind of incubation?

00:06:59.094 --> 00:07:02.108
- Virtually all of the
interesting apps now came from

00:07:02.108 --> 00:07:06.436
a combination of an
acquisition and a 20% time.

00:07:06.436 --> 00:07:08.409
If you look at Maps, if
you look at Google Earth,

00:07:08.409 --> 00:07:12.060
if you look at Chrome and
Android, all of them came from

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:14.867
somebody trying something,
identifying something,

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:17.530
and then we would say, we
have all these 20%-timers

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:19.000
but we need a real group.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:19.833
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:07:19.833 --> 00:07:21.369
- And the fastest way to do that was to

00:07:21.369 --> 00:07:23.350
create a real group or buy a company.

00:07:23.350 --> 00:07:25.943
- What's the most important change,

00:07:25.943 --> 00:07:27.018
and most significant change in your way

00:07:27.018 --> 00:07:30.685
of thinking about the
world over the last...

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:32.813
20 years?

00:07:36.899 --> 00:07:40.334
- That the impossible can happen.

00:07:40.334 --> 00:07:42.584
I never thought that the Soviet Union

00:07:42.584 --> 00:07:44.584
would implode so easily.

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:50.049
And I never thought the
Chinese would abandon

00:07:52.586 --> 00:07:56.610
the communist system that had moved into

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:58.860
the free market so readily.

00:08:00.509 --> 00:08:03.176
It was unthinkable 20 years ago.

00:08:04.866 --> 00:08:09.189
And both have happened,
the world has changed.

00:08:09.189 --> 00:08:12.534
- And it's not clear exactly
how it's all going to...?

00:08:12.534 --> 00:08:16.820
- No, it is not exactly
clear when it will happen-

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:18.512
- [Charlie] Exactly.

00:08:18.512 --> 00:08:21.728
- But that it will happen
now in the long term,

00:08:21.728 --> 00:08:23.994
50 to 100 years, yes.

00:08:23.994 --> 00:08:26.767
- [Charlie] And the center of
gravity is shifting to Asia.

00:08:26.767 --> 00:08:29.433
- It must be, because
the population is there.

00:08:29.433 --> 00:08:33.850
The talent pool of 1.3 million
people plus the Japanese,

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:37.683
the Koreans and the
Vietnamese and the others,

00:08:38.967 --> 00:08:42.055
it can match Europe and America.

00:08:42.055 --> 00:08:45.235
But the talent pool was inert.

00:08:45.235 --> 00:08:47.119
It did not have science and technology,

00:08:47.119 --> 00:08:50.065
did not care about science and technology.

00:08:50.065 --> 00:08:52.648
But now everything that you do,

00:08:55.291 --> 00:08:56.414
Asia's doing.

00:08:56.414 --> 00:08:59.414
(heavy rock guitar)

00:09:04.035 --> 00:09:07.076
- Lou's records is a very important place,

00:09:07.076 --> 00:09:10.792
it's one of the most famous
record stores in San Diego,

00:09:10.792 --> 00:09:14.244
and one of the most famous in the country,

00:09:14.244 --> 00:09:16.736
and when Blink first
started, I drove around in

00:09:16.736 --> 00:09:18.714
a 20-mile radius of the store

00:09:18.714 --> 00:09:21.766
and I broke into every
high school at night,

00:09:21.766 --> 00:09:24.524
and I made Blink flyers and I hung 'em

00:09:24.524 --> 00:09:27.525
in every single locker
in all these high schools

00:09:27.525 --> 00:09:30.192
that we were playing at the club downtown.

00:09:30.192 --> 00:09:33.202
At that point in time,
everyone in San Diego

00:09:33.202 --> 00:09:34.896
wanted to support the local bands,

00:09:34.896 --> 00:09:36.722
it was just a really great scene.

00:09:36.722 --> 00:09:40.240
So because I put those
flyers in those lockers,

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:44.240
we ended up having our
first show at a big club,

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.982
all the people came,
and we had enough people

00:09:47.982 --> 00:09:49.980
that watched us that the
guy that owned the club,

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:54.040
invited us the following week
to play on the big stage.

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:56.025
So what we did, is not
only played that show,

00:09:56.025 --> 00:09:58.051
we rushed and made a
really quick recording,

00:09:58.051 --> 00:09:59.523
it was our first recording,

00:09:59.523 --> 00:10:00.756
with a little Buddha statue on it,

00:10:00.756 --> 00:10:03.569
and people commonly refer
to that record as Buddha,

00:10:03.569 --> 00:10:06.554
we made that to sell here in this store,

00:10:06.554 --> 00:10:09.984
so we would put five tapes in at a time,

00:10:09.984 --> 00:10:11.970
it was a time when tapes were selling,

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:14.786
and every week we would
call up and they were gone!

00:10:14.786 --> 00:10:16.720
Come in the next week with
five more, they're gone.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:18.447
Then we gave 'em 10, they're gone.

00:10:18.447 --> 00:10:20.504
And then gave 'em 20, and
the next thing you know,

00:10:20.504 --> 00:10:22.675
we've sold thousands of
these tape cassettes,

00:10:22.675 --> 00:10:25.939
all of these records, and
then we got our start,

00:10:25.939 --> 00:10:29.535
it was little suburban
kids, we had a dream,

00:10:29.535 --> 00:10:32.445
to be in the punk rock section.

00:10:32.445 --> 00:10:36.700
And I'm here now looking at
all these things I grew up on,

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:39.512
and they're so insanely important to me.

00:10:39.512 --> 00:10:40.654
- [Interviewer] Do you ever visualize you

00:10:40.654 --> 00:10:41.903
winning anything again?

00:10:41.903 --> 00:10:46.079
- Always. Always dreamt
of winning the World Cup.

00:10:46.079 --> 00:10:47.746
Hasn't happened yet.

00:10:51.519 --> 00:10:53.436
Still look back to '98,

00:10:54.769 --> 00:10:56.224
after the red card that

00:10:56.224 --> 00:10:58.288
I got against Argentina,

00:10:58.288 --> 00:11:02.098
what went on in my life and in
my family's life after that,

00:11:02.098 --> 00:11:04.061
I think it was very tough.

00:11:04.061 --> 00:11:07.953
It was probably the toughest
moment of my career.

00:11:07.953 --> 00:11:10.555
I was having death
threats, I never felt safe

00:11:10.555 --> 00:11:12.815
for three and a half years.

00:11:12.815 --> 00:11:15.519
People used to turn around
and saying, "Well you've let

00:11:15.519 --> 00:11:17.354
"your country down, and
you've let your family down,

00:11:17.354 --> 00:11:18.963
"so how does that feel?"

00:11:18.963 --> 00:11:21.252
And honestly, I never
felt as alone as that,

00:11:21.252 --> 00:11:22.728
as a person, as a footballer.

00:11:22.728 --> 00:11:27.669
It can knock a person down so
much that they just go under.

00:11:27.669 --> 00:11:32.150
Outside pubs in London there
was effigies hung of me,

00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:35.381
and this was on the
front of the newspaper.

00:11:35.381 --> 00:11:39.548
It's just something that sticks
in my mind from that time.

00:11:42.522 --> 00:11:45.285
Something they all said
about me at the time,

00:11:45.285 --> 00:11:49.452
there was a headline of 10
lions, one stupid little boy.

00:11:50.424 --> 00:11:51.635
- [Interviewer] Still
emotional, isn't it, still raw?

00:11:51.635 --> 00:11:52.468
- Yeah.

00:11:57.990 --> 00:12:00.033
This is a saying that I use all the time,

00:12:00.033 --> 00:12:02.446
and it's true, it is a round world.

00:12:02.446 --> 00:12:05.050
'98 was just before the World
Cup when I was at the top,

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:08.554
and then after the World
Cup I was at the bottom.

00:12:08.554 --> 00:12:10.227
And then you work yourself back up.

00:12:10.227 --> 00:12:13.474
The upside for me was the Greece game.

00:12:13.474 --> 00:12:16.057
(bright piano)

00:12:16.943 --> 00:12:19.277
Once the game started it was the start of

00:12:19.277 --> 00:12:21.645
an incredible day for me.

00:12:21.645 --> 00:12:24.295
It was even going to
the World Cup that day

00:12:24.295 --> 00:12:26.717
or it was going into qualifying games

00:12:26.717 --> 00:12:28.813
which none of us wanted to do because

00:12:28.813 --> 00:12:31.261
the expectations of us, I remember

00:12:31.261 --> 00:12:33.986
getting a free kick on the edge of the box

00:12:33.986 --> 00:12:35.679
and I remember putting the ball down

00:12:35.679 --> 00:12:38.037
and I remember looking up
at the clock and thinking,

00:12:38.037 --> 00:12:40.186
this is it, you know,
this is the only chance

00:12:40.186 --> 00:12:41.526
I'm going to get now.

00:12:41.526 --> 00:12:44.082
The only thing I could hear was the man

00:12:44.082 --> 00:12:48.002
and his drum round about here, I think.

00:12:48.002 --> 00:12:49.858
And now step back, took deep breaths,

00:12:49.858 --> 00:12:53.508
run up, and as soon as it
left my foot that was it.

00:12:53.508 --> 00:12:56.682
(bright piano)

00:12:56.682 --> 00:12:59.504
It was the loudest I think
I've ever heard the fans,

00:12:59.504 --> 00:13:03.486
it was such a huge moment for everyone.

00:13:03.486 --> 00:13:06.649
I remember just running
off and being that excited,

00:13:06.649 --> 00:13:08.341
just jumping up in the air, you know,

00:13:08.341 --> 00:13:09.896
I could have touched
the top of the stadium

00:13:09.896 --> 00:13:13.078
if I wanted to, because I felt that tall.

00:13:13.078 --> 00:13:17.191
(dramatic sustained piano)

00:13:17.191 --> 00:13:20.085
Right, the whole canvas
is the idea of the goal,

00:13:20.085 --> 00:13:22.466
there's the boy in the
corner, my celebration,

00:13:22.466 --> 00:13:26.159
and the words belief,
strength, and family,

00:13:26.159 --> 00:13:30.326
what I needed, what I had
to get through after '98.

00:13:32.222 --> 00:13:33.267
(piano flourish)

00:13:33.267 --> 00:13:34.600
Finishes it off.

00:13:36.228 --> 00:13:38.490
Being in front of a blank piece of paper

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:40.548
with experts around you as well,

00:13:40.548 --> 00:13:42.610
I think that is much more daunting,

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:43.943
than stepping out in front of

00:13:43.943 --> 00:13:45.635
90,000 people playing football.

00:13:45.635 --> 00:13:48.468
(uplifting piano)

00:13:49.329 --> 00:13:50.844
- Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:13:50.844 --> 00:13:52.355
I hope you enjoyed the
video, I'd love to know,

00:13:52.355 --> 00:13:53.826
what did you think?

00:13:53.826 --> 00:13:55.886
What was the single biggest
takeaway that you took

00:13:55.886 --> 00:13:58.272
from this video that you're
going to apply to your life,

00:13:58.272 --> 00:13:59.865
or to your business somehow.

00:13:59.865 --> 00:14:01.701
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:14:01.701 --> 00:14:03.467
If you're within the first
couple hours of this video

00:14:03.467 --> 00:14:04.893
going live, you have a
chance to win one of two

00:14:04.893 --> 00:14:06.334
daily prizes as well.

00:14:06.334 --> 00:14:08.383
I also want to give a quick
shoutout to Frank Hoffmann.

00:14:08.383 --> 00:14:10.971
Frank, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:14:10.971 --> 00:14:13.275
Your One Word, and posting it on Twitter,

00:14:13.275 --> 00:14:15.021
I really really appreciate
the support, man,

00:14:15.021 --> 00:14:16.818
and I hope you enjoyed the read.

00:14:16.818 --> 00:14:17.966
So thank you guys again for watching,

00:14:17.966 --> 00:14:19.115
I believe in you.

00:14:19.115 --> 00:14:20.986
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:14:20.986 --> 00:14:23.290
and whatever your one word is.

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:25.191
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:14:25.191 --> 00:14:28.074
(electronic whoosh)

